---

@table tb-parts
title: Who gets which license

| Part | License | File |
|---|---|---|
| Renderer, parser, validator | Apache License 2.0 | `LICENSE` |
| Future SDK, MCP client and CLI | Apache License 2.0 | `LICENSE` |
| Specification text (`spec/`) | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0) | `spec/LICENSE` |
| Examples (`examples/`) | Apache License 2.0 | `LICENSE` |
@@

@heading h-why
text: Why Apache-2.0
level: 1

Apache-2.0 lets anyone use, modify and ship the tools, including in closed products, as long as they keep the license and the `NOTICE` file. It also includes an explicit **patent grant**: every contributor licenses the patents their contribution needs, and that license ends for anyone who sues over those patents. For a format that should be implemented by many independent tools, that protection matters more than a shorter license text.
@@

@heading h-spec
text: Why CC BY 4.0 for the specification
level: 1

Anyone may copy, translate and adapt the specification, including to write a competing implementation, as long as they credit the source. A format only spreads if implementers can quote its rules freely.
@@

@heading h-contrib
text: Contributions: DCO, no CLA
level: 1

Contributions come in under the same license they go out under (Apache-2.0 for code, CC BY 4.0 for spec text). The `Signed-off-by` line of the [Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/) records that you have the right to submit the work. No contributor license agreement is needed for this repository.
@@

@note n-server
type: alcance

Some hosted services built on the format are licensed differently and live in separate repositories, which may ask for a contributor license agreement. That does not change anything here: everything in this repository stays Apache-2.0 or CC BY 4.0.
@@

@heading h-mark
text: Name and marks
level: 1

Apache-2.0 does not grant rights to names or logos (section 6). You may say a tool «reads LANDDY `.lnd` files». A trademark policy and a «LANDDY compatible» mark tied to the test fixtures are planned.
@@
